{"slug":"INNERRANGE","companyName":"Inner Range ANZ","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/inner-range-anz","fetchedAt":"2026-11-16T22:10:56Z","followerCount":3180,"bio":"Inner Range is a manufacturer of integrated Video, Access Control and Security solutions. Founded in Melbourne, Australia, Inner Range has over 35 years of innovation and has more than 150,000 systems deployed globally.\n \nWe are passionate about empowering our customers to protect what they value most, their property, their possessions and most importantly \u2013 their people.\n \nWe manufacture end-to-end solutions from the card you badge at one of our readers to the controller securing the door, right through to the enterprise security management software monitoring multiple sites anywhere in the world. Our scalable products are suitable for high-end residential, commercial and enterprise sites across verticals such as education, healthcare, government and critical infrastructure.\n \nOur continual investment in research and development puts our products at the forefront of access control, security, video and smart building technology. We partner with best-in-class providers of adjacent technologies such as intercom, payroll, building automation and incorporate the latest in AI technology with solutions for facial recognition, biometrics, number plate recognition and many more. With over 120 native integrations to 3rd party systems and open integration pathways, we provide our customers with a unified system behind a single pane of glass.\n \nInner Range offers our partners a range of competency-based training courses to ensure the best experience with our products and outcomes for their customers. Additionally, our global support team ensures that any issues are resolved quickly with minimal impact to the end user.\n \nFrom entry to enterprise, Inner Range provides an end-to-end security solution capable of addressing the most difficult building management needs, providing peace of mind for you and your people.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-11-09","text":"Security without compromise.\nInner Range Global is proud to announce that Infiniti Class 5 Control Equipment has been independently re-certified by ASIAL through to 2 October 2028.\nThe renewed Class 5 certification confirms Infiniti\u2019s capability against AS/NZS 2201.1:2007, supporting high-security applications where robust protection is critical.\nFrom government and defence facilities to critical infrastructure, financial institutions and other high-security environments, Infiniti delivers the flexibility to manage Class 5 high-security zones alongside standard commercial-grade security areas within one unified platform.\nOne platform. Multiple security levels. Built for environments where security matters most.\nFor more info: https://lnkd.in/eaxwiVGk\n#InnerRange #Infiniti #Class5 #ASIAL\n#Security #AccessControl #IntrusionDetection\n#HighSecurity #CriticalInfrastructure","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/inner-range-anz/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-26","text":"Join Inner Range Global at the Security & Government Expo (SAGE) 2026 and discover how government, defence, and critical infrastructure organisations are strengthening security with a unified platform for access control, automation, and real-time monitoring.\nBuilt for high-security environments, Inner Range has been protecting government, defence, and critical infrastructure for over a decade. Our Class 5 certified Infiniti security platform delivers advanced access control, encrypted intrusion detection, unified video surveillance, and real-time monitoring, which provide optimal security protection.\nSee the latest innovations in Integriti and learn how Inner Range helps organisations improve security, streamline operations, and gain greater control across complex environments.\nThursday 19 November 2026 | Booth 28\nHotel Realm, Canberra\nEvent Info: https://lnkd.in/ekyJ_bMA\nWe look forward to connecting with security professionals and discussing the future of high-security management sol","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/inner-range-anz/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-26","text":"We had a fantastic first day at the CANASA Central security show. Come on in and chat with the Inner Range Global team and the team from Omni-Tech Solution Services about our unified and integrated access, video and intrusion solutions that span from entry level single site right up to enterprise grade multisite deployments.\nLive demo's, great conversations, broaden your horizons.\nCatch us tomorrow at booth 1030 before it's all over for another year.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/inner-range-anz/home/","repostOf":"Inner Range Americas"}]}
## 2026-11-16T22:10:15Z GALLAGHER
{"slug":"GALLAGHER","companyName":"Gallagher Security","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security","fetchedAt":"2026-11-16T22:10:15Z","followerCount":33892,"bio":"Gallagher Security is a global leader in integrated technology solutions that help organizations around the world protect, secure, and manage people and assets. Our award-winning solutions are trusted by government, defense, commercial, industrial, healthcare, transportation, mining, and educational organizations in 140 countries.\n\nWe design and manufacture a comprehensive suite of security software and hardware - including integrated access control, intruder alarm, and perimeter solutions - all on site at our global headquarters. The intelligent technology can be scaled and customized to deliver business efficiencies across simple, enterprise, and high security sites.\n\nTrusted by over 20,000 security customers worldwide, Gallagher solutions are used to simplify life on campus within the education sector, keep staff and patients safe in healthcare, ensure the highest security requirements and compliances are met for government sites in the Five Eyes alliance, safeguard critical infrastructure within the utilities industry, and ensure uninterrupted movement for transport and logistics.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-11-16","text":"Your visitor experience starts long before anyone reaches your site.\nFrom the moment someone registers online to the moment they leave, every step shapes how they see your business.\nCreate an exceptional first impression. Swipe through the five steps to a seamless visitor journey.\nWant to know more about Gallagher Security Visitor Management, powered by Kenai? Book a demo: https://lnkd.in/eXE54fYE","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-13","text":"A widespread Microsoft service disruption is affecting email access for organisations around the world, including Gallagher. This means there may be delays in our teams receiving or responding to emails. We appreciate your patience and understanding. If you need to contact us urgently, please contact your Gallagher representative by phone. We'll provide an update in the comments once normal service has resumed.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-09","text":"What happens when physical security becomes an IT responsibility?\nThat's the question we've been exploring throughout In The Know, our podcast for security and IT professionals navigating a rapidly changing industry, and all six episodes and companion blogs are now available.\nAs access control systems become increasingly connected to wider technology ecosystems, security and IT teams are finding themselves working closer together than ever before.\nHosted by Tim Orr and Kusania Cairns, each episode is a short, practical conversation designed to help security and IT professionals understand the trends shaping the industry, while our companion blogs provide actionable takeaways.\nWhether you're responsible for security, IT infrastructure, cyber resilience, facilities, or digital transformation, this series offers insights you can take back to your organisation.\nListen now on now on Spotify and Apple Podcasts, and check out the companion blogs here: https://lnkd.in/efqefxWU\nSpotify: https:/","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-02","text":"One Unified View for Smarter Operational Intelligence\nBring Gallagher access control, perimeter security and alarm management into Synergy for streamlined operations and improved situational awareness.\nhttps://lnkd.in/e7x68vtF","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-02","text":"We're incredibly proud to share that Gallagher Security's Date of Warranty Report has been recognised at the 2026 Australian Security Industry Association Limited (ASIAL) Awards for Excellence.\nLaunched as part of Command Centre v9.30, the report gives End Users and Channel Partners greater visibility of the hardware installed across their sites, helping them understand device age and warranty status and make more informed decisions about future upgrades.\n\"The best innovations come from listening to our End Users and Channel Partners and solving real-world challenges,\" says Craig Schutte, Executive Vice President APAC and IMEA. \"This recognition is especially meaningful because the Date of Warranty Report was developed to address a genuine need in the market and deliver greater value to those who use our solutions every day.\"\nThe recognition made an already special evening even more memorable as #TeamGallagher joined the industry in celebrating the 30th anniversary of the Australian Se","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security/home/"}]}
## 2026-11-16T22:09:34Z JOHNSON
{"slug":"JOHNSON","companyName":"Johnson Controls","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls","fetchedAt":"2026-11-16T22:09:34Z","followerCount":3832496,"bio":"Johnson Controls is a global leader in thermal management, mission-critical building systems, energy efficiency and decarbonization. We help our customers use energy more productively, reduce carbon emissions and operate with the precision and resilience required in rapidly expanding industries such as data centers, healthcare, pharmaceuticals, advanced manufacturing and higher education.\n\nFor more than 140 years, Johnson Controls has been delivering performance where it really matters. Backed by advanced technology, lifecycle services and an industry-leading field organization, we elevate customer performance, turning goals into real-world results and helping move society forward.\n\nVisit johnsoncontrols.com for more information.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-11-16","text":"AI is changing the thermal demands placed on today's data centers, requiring operators to think beyond traditional cooling approaches.\nAnd supporting next-generation AI-workloads starts with critical decisions around capacity planning and technology selection.\nExplore some of the key considerations for designing AI-ready data centers: https://on.jci.com/4AJCVqT","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-16","text":"On\u2011site power generation using gas engines and turbines is quickly becoming a viable substitute for grid electricity in district energy applications. And one big benefit is the potential to capture the waste heat produced by these systems, doubling their efficiency and reducing primary energy consumption by up to 20%.\nFind out how this is accomplished in the new \"Behind-the-meter Cooling\" webinar produced in conjunction with the International District Energy Association (IDEA) and featuring Adrian Marticorena and Rajesh Dixit from Johnson Controls.\nJoin us November 18 to learn more. Register today to save your spot: https://on.jci.com/4C2Crgc","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-12","text":"What could more intelligent and connected building operations look like for your organization? \ud83e\udd14\nCome find out at IFMA World Workplace 2026! Stop by Booth #1803 on November 18\u201319 to connect with our experts, experience live demos, and talk through your biggest facility and workplace challenges.\nSee how technology can help turn building data into better decisions, more efficient operations, and stronger outcomes: https://on.jci.com/4zqMvOz\n\ud83d\udccd Booth 1803 | Anaheim, CA\n\ud83d\udcc5 November 18\u201319","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-12","text":"Data center capacity needs are changing fast. How can operators scale AI infrastructure rapidly, wherever it's needed?\nJoin the Data Centre Magazine webinar for a deep-dive on modular data centers and how modular approaches can help organizations deploy AI factory capacity faster, more predictably and more efficiently.\nRegister here: https://on.jci.com/4zc664K","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-10","text":"Could waste heat help support your next phase of data center growth?\nSee how you can unlock additional AI capacity with Reference Design Guide 407, which is focused on thermally driven absorption chillers with on-site power generation.\nThis outline can help you reduce your cooling electrical demand by up to 44% to return 97MW in compute power or lower CO\u2082 emissions by up to 43%.\nDownload the guide here: https://on.jci.com/46bgQ7d","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"}]}
## 2026-11-16T22:08:51Z NZPOLICE
{"slug":"NZPOLICE","companyName":"NZ Police","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/nz-police","fetchedAt":"2026-11-16T22:08:51Z","followerCount":29849,"bio":"New Zealand Police is the lead agency responsible for reducing crime and enhancing community safety. With over 15,000 staff, we provide policing services 24 hours a day and function from 371 community-based police stations around the country.\n\nWe operate by land, sea and air, and respond to more than 600,000 emergency 111 calls each year.\n\nSafer Communities Together.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-11-14","text":"Drive like somebody is watching \ud83d\udc40\nHint: it\u2019s us.\n87\n2\n2\n\u200b\nFeed post","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/nz-police/posts/"},{"date":"2026-11-12","text":"The New Zealand Police Be Safe, Feel Safe booklet is now available in 29 languages \ud83c\udf0e\nFrom disasters and emergencies to family and personal safety, this booklet contains our latest safety information as well as where to get support and how to contact police.\nFeeling safe starts with having the right information, in a language you understand. Check it out here https://lnkd.in/erVQAWRM","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/nz-police/posts/"},{"date":"2026-11-13","text":"Two men have been arrested and face more than 20 drug and firearm related charges following a huge haul of guns, drugs, cash, gold and cars by Wellington Police.\nFollowing a two-day search of two properties, a huge haul was discovered. It included GHB (gamma-hydroxybutyrate), cannabis, a kilo of methamphetamine in distinctive wrapping worth approximately $105,000, and space vape liquid and packaging.\nCases of cash estimated to be carrying more than $100,000, gold bars and $50,000 of gold coins, a large recycling bin full of copper, a rifle, a 3D printed firearm and 9 classics cars including a limousine, a Chevrolet Bel Air and a Plymouth Savoy were also recovered by Police.\nThe seizures follow nearly a year\u2019s worth of investigating.\nDetective Senior Seargeant Lee Underhill says the seizure represents a big blow to the Wellington drug trade.\n\"One of the men has been supplying a wide range of illicit drugs from his property for many years, benefitting off the addiction of others,\u201d she sa","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/nz-police/posts/"}]}
## 2026-11-16T22:08:11Z ASIS
{"slug":"ASIS","companyName":"ASIS International","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international","fetchedAt":"2026-11-16T22:08:11Z","followerCount":103066,"bio":"The world's largest association for security professionals, ASIS International has 243 chapters around the globe. Wherever you are in your career, whether just getting started or a seasoned security professional, ASIS International has the tools, information, and global network you need to achieve your goals. Put the power of ASIS to work for you.  www.asisonline.org","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-03-21","text":"Our #MyASIS community is unmatched. We are in awe of our members\u2019 dedication to the profession and each other, who are always looking for ways to support their colleagues and friends. In honor of Membership Appreciation Month we ask that you share your appreciation for your fellow members, maybe someone who has influenced your career or helped you in your ASIS journey? Tag a member in the comments below and be entered to win a FREE GSX All-Access Pass to #GSX2026. #ASISMemberAppreciation","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-16","text":"Building an effective security metrics program, operationalizing AI in the GSOC, and recovering from trauma beyond the uniform: three ASIS community events you won\u2019t want to miss this month. Catch up on ASIS Community Pulse for November.\nLearn more on the ASIS blog: https://bit.ly/4fxfUOS\n#ASISBlog #SecurityProfessional #ASISCommunity","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-11","text":"This Veterans Day, we honor the men and women who served, and the sacrifice, discipline, and duty that came with it.\nTo the veterans who now carry that same commitment into the security profession, protecting people, places, and communities every day, thank you from ASIS International.\n#VeteransDay #SecurityProfessionals","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-13","text":"What do the most resilient threat management programs have in common?\nGood intelligence. Multidisciplinary judgment. Practical intervention options. Sustained leadership support.\nTechnology can help identify and organize concerning information, but human judgment is still essential for context, assessing behavior, and deciding on a response.\nRead the full article from Security Management on the ASIS website: https://lnkd.in/gEjhsRKU\nAuthor: Claire Meyer\n#ThreatAssessment #SecurityManagement #ASISInternational","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-13","text":"220+ security leaders. 24 countries. One sold-out conference.\nThe 2026 ASIS International Asia Pacific Conference gathered the global security community to Singapore to discuss emerging threats, organizational resilience, and responsible technology to show how security helps enable business.\n\ud83d\udccd Next stop is New Delhi, 14-15 October 2027.\nhttps://lnkd.in/d4sCczUM\n#ASISAPAC2027 #ASISAPAC #ASISInternational","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"}]}
## 2026-11-16T22:07:30Z NZSA
{"slug":"NZSA","companyName":"New Zealand Security Association (NZSA)","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/new-zealand-security-association","fetchedAt":"2026-11-16T22:07:30Z","followerCount":3765,"bio":"The New Zealand Security Association (NZSA) is the largest industry representative body for the security industry in New Zealand and represents over 85% of the industry by revenue. Its voluntary members include security providers ranging from large multi-nationals to sole traders and also includes individuals and companies who are not direct providers of security services but have an interest in the industry.\nThe stated objective of the New Zealand Security Association is to do all things necessary and lawful to ensure there is always available to the New Zealand public, a security industry comprising of persons and firms who are fit and proper. The New Zealand Security Association is committed to the highest standards of professional and ethical conduct at all times.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-11-09","text":"Protecting crowded places is a subject close to our hearts at the NZSA. Having hosted two Crowded Places Forums, we\u2019ve seen the value of bringing people together to share knowledge and strengthen our collective approach to public safety.\nASIS New Zealand\u2019s upcoming session with NZ Police will be a valuable opportunity to continue that conversation and gain practical insights into keeping our crowded places safer.\nFor those working in this area, CrowdSafeNZ is a great source of practical guidance and resources to support safer crowded places: https://lnkd.in/e7BZqs-j","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/new-zealand-security-association/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-02","text":"A great overview  of the 'why' behind the new New Zealand Security Association Advanced Security Officer training programme\nThanks DEFSEC New Zealand and Nicholas Dynon.\nYou can find out more about the training here, along with our good practice guidelines for citizen's arrest: https://lnkd.in/e2BZeMm6\n#CitizensArrest\n#SecurityIndustry","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/new-zealand-security-association/home/"}]}
## 2026-11-16T22:06:48Z ASISNZ
{"slug":"ASISNZ","companyName":"ASIS New Zealand","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-new-zealand","fetchedAt":"2026-11-16T22:06:48Z","followerCount":175,"bio":"ASIS New Zealand is part of ASIS International Group 15, region 15A. There are over 130 members of ASIS International based in New Zealand alone.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-11-12","text":"\ud83e\udd1d Executive Committee Re-elected! \ud83e\udd1d\nWe are incredibly grateful and humbled by the NZ security community for unanimously re-electing us to lead the ASIS International New Zealand Chapter for another term. Thank you for your continued trust and support! \ud83c\uddf3\ud83c\uddff\ud83d\udd12\nPlease join us in congratulating our re-elected Executive Committee:\n\ud83d\udd39 Andy Gollings \u2013 Chair\n\ud83d\udd39 Arjen Bloem SRMP-C I APP\u00ae \u2013 Deputy Chair\n\ud83d\udd39 Dee Wakelin \u2013 Treasurer\n\ud83d\udd39Reck Reck \u2013 Secretary\nWe are absolutely thrilled to carry on as your executive team. Our mission remains clear: to actively grow, support, and connect our incredible security community across Aotearoa.\nWe\u2019re looking forward to another fantastic year of collaboration, networking, and professional development.\n\ud83d\udce2 Stay tuned\u2014we\u2019ll be sharing more details about our wonderful Liaisons very soon!\nLet\u2019s make this next year our best one yet.\n#ASISNZ #ASISInternational #SecurityCommunity #SecurityLeaders #ExecutiveCommittee #Networking #ProfessionalDevelopment #AotearoaSecurity","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-new-zealand/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-12","text":"Speaker update: we are pleased to confirm that Paul McAven (Christchurch City Council) has joined the speaker lineup alongside Senior Sergeant Gareth Brown (NZ Police) for our upcoming November Chapter Meeting: Protecting Our Crowded Places.\n\ud83c\udf9f\ufe0f Register now: https://lnkd.in/eepqSnVp\nAs metropolitan centres expand and major public events draw increasingly concentrated crowds, protective security at the intersection of venue operations and civic infrastructure faces unprecedented operational complexity.\nManaging risk across these dynamic environments moves well beyond baseline regulatory compliance, it demands data-informed vulnerability assessments, integrated multi-agency communication protocols, and agile incident response models.\nTo deliver both doctrine-level strategy and empirical operational takeaways, this session examines the crowded places ecosystem through two critical lenses:\n\u2022 Strategic Threat Landscapes & Counter-Terrorism Preparedness | Senior Sergeant Gareth Brown (New Ze","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-new-zealand/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-09","text":"We are pleased to announce our next ASIS New Zealand Chapter meeting this November, focusing on one of the most critical topics facing our sector: Protecting our Crowded Places, with NZ Police.\nFrom retail precincts and corporate towers to major public events and transport hubs, crowded places remain dynamic environments where public safety, threat mitigation, and operational resilience intersect.\nFor security executives, facility managers, and risk leaders, understanding New Zealand\u2019s national protective security framework is essential to safeguarding our communities and mitigating emerging threats.\nJoin us for an exclusive lunchtime session featuring direct operational insights on practical risk management, cross-sector collaboration, and key strategies for venue and facility protection.\nFeatured Guest Speaker\nSenior Sergeant Gareth Brown \u2013 New Zealand Police\nWith over 25 years of dedicated service in the New Zealand Police and a strong operational foundation from his prior service i","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-new-zealand/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-02","text":"The final stretch of the year is always fast-paced, but our security community continues to operate at full throttle.\nReflecting on last week\u2019s chapter meeting, the room was buzzing with critical insights, policy updates, and forward-looking discussions shaping the future of security in New Zealand:\n\u2022 Hon. Mark Mitchell shared key legislative updates and recent government milestones, including progress on the Move-on Orders legislation, new police recruitment numbers, and targeted actions addressing financial crime.\n\u2022 Gary Morrison, CEO at the New Zealand Security Association (NZSA), provided essential industry updates, highlighting recent PSPLA developments and collaborative work with MBIE regarding access-controlled doors.\n\u2022 Andy Gollings, our ASIS NZ Chairperson and CEO at Red Badge Group, delivered an essential briefing on emergency preparedness, a critical priority for every security professional navigating today's threat landscape.\nA huge thank you to our guest speakers, as well ","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-new-zealand/home/"},{"date":"2026-08-18","text":"We\u2019re capturing the insights from our chapter meetings into in-depth articles so our community can access actionable security intelligence long after the session ends.\nOur inaugural article stems from our June meeting on Executive Protection in a Corporate Environment, featuring guest speakers Mark Richards and Ray Millar.\nDrawing on decades of experience across NZ Police, Diplomatic Protection, the US Dept of State DSS, and major financial institutions, Mark and Ray break down why corporate EP is a critical business continuity strategy \u2014 not just a C-suite privilege.\n#ASISNZ #ProtectiveSecurity #ExecutiveProtection #SecurityLeadership #ThoughtLeadership #RiskManagement","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-new-zealand/home/"}]}
