## 2026-11-08T23:19:14Z JACQUES
{"slug":"JACQUES","companyName":"Jacques Technologies","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/jacques","fetchedAt":"2026-11-08T23:19:14Z","followerCount":0,"bio":"","recentPosts":[]}
## 2026-11-08T23:18:38Z ICT
{"slug":"ICT","companyName":"Integrated Control Technology (ICT)","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology","fetchedAt":"2026-11-08T23:18:38Z","followerCount":28712,"bio":"Integrated Control Technology (ICT) is a world leading manufacturer of unified electronic access control and security solutions enabling a scalable solution for organizations to protect their people, operations and information.\n\nICT's Protege\u00ae seamlessly integrates a full suite of security management functions and technologies using an open architecture design. offering electronic access control, ID credential issuance and management; alarm monitoring, apartment management, digital video surveillance and management, real-time digital video content analysis, integration of biometric technologies, intrusion detection and smart card functionality, plus integration with a multitude of third-party systems.\n\nBased in Auckland, New Zealand, ICT has a global presence with offices located in Denver (Colorado USA), Amersham (United Kingdom), and Sydney (Australia) to provide full local sales, support and service to our clients and partners around the world.\n\nTo learn more, visit www.ict.co","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-11-06","text":"\"It means we now don't have to have a manager onsite.\"\nThat's Terry King, Managing Director of Safeguard, on the Protege GX system installed by Millennium Technology. At Safeguard, a new customer has their PIN seconds after registering and paying.\nRead the full case study here: https://lnkd.in/gehgySpq\n#GC26 #ICT","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-05","text":"Nobody could say who had the keys to the city truck.\nThat was a real problem for the City of Mooresville. Shared vehicle keys went missing, and there was no record of who took them or when.\nThe fix was key management tied to the badge staff already carry. They check out keys with their Protege GX credentials and every checkout is logged. Help desk can confirm a key is available before dispatching anyone.\nThe same system now handles facial readers on the Police Department evidence room and remote scheduling for park gates and bathrooms. Fewer trips to unlock and lock by hand.\nUnlock the full potential of your access control solution by partnering with ICT. Read the full case study here  \ud83d\udc49 https://lnkd.in/gYbwm99n","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-04","text":"Every site you quote asks something different of an access control system.\n> At a bank branch it\u2019s tellers who can raise a silent duress alarm and a vault that only opens for two authorised people.\n> On a logistics site it\u2019s knowing which trucks are booked and who\u2019s still on site when the fire alarm sounds.\n> And in a data centre it\u2019s stopping tailgating before anyone reaches the data hall.\nProtege GX covers all three, with access control, intrusion detection and building automation working together, so your techs learn one system across all of them.\nBen Italiano and Jacky Chow will be on Stand 1928 at The Security Event Asia to talk through whichever one you\u2019re working on.\n#TSEAsia #ICT","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-02","text":"A logistics site has trucks queuing at the gate, drivers and contractors coming and going and doors opening at every dock, all at the same time.\nAt The Security Event Asia we\u2019re running a live demo of a site like it on Protege GX, integrated with Hikvision MinMoe facial recognition.\nA driver is recognised at the gate and a pressure plate picks up the truck, and when a dock door is held open the alarm and the camera come up together.\nIf you\u2019re quoting a port, depot or distribution centre, Ben Italiano and Jacky Chow will be on Stand 1928 - 10 to 12 November.\n#TSEAsia #ICT","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-11-05","text":"Thank you to Stratel (Malaysia) Sdn. Bhd. and Camnix for hosting the Smart Solutions Workshop in Kuching on Wednesday, and to everyone who joined us at Lot10 Boutique Hotel!\nOur Director of Sales for Asia, Jacky Chow, took the room through Protege GX, from system overview to design and programming.\nSessions from AxxonSoft on video management and CALMS Technologies Sdn Bhd on visitor management and facility booking ran alongside. The live demos kept conversations going at the tables between sessions.\nIt was a great morning in Kuching, and we\u2019re looking forward to the next one.\n#SmartSolutionsWorkshop #ICT","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"}]}
## 2026-11-08T23:17:56Z BOSCH
{"slug":"BOSCH","companyName":"Bosch Security and Safety Systems","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/bosch-security-systems","fetchedAt":"2026-11-08T23:17:56Z","followerCount":48222,"bio":"This LinkedIn page for Bosch Security and Safety Systems is no longer active.\nThe business has been acquired by Triton and is now part of the Keenfinity Group, an independent company delivering professional communication and security solutions that connect and protect people and assets. Keenfinity Group combines leading brands and expertise across Audio, Video Systems, Intrusion & Access, and Electronics Manufacturing Services (EMS), serving customers worldwide.\n\nTo continue receiving product updates, insights, and news, please follow our dedicated LinkedIn pages: \n\u2022 Video Systems: IQSIGHT https://www.linkedin.com/company/iqsight\n\u2022 Intrusion & Access: Radionix https://www.linkedin.com/company/radionix\n\u2022 Conference Solutions | Keenfinity Group https://www.linkedin.com/company/bosch-conference-solutions\n\u2022 Public Address & Voice Alarm | Keenfinity Group https://www.linkedin.com/company/public-address-solutions\n\nMore information: www.keenfinity-group.com","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-07-11","text":"\u203c\ufe0fImportant update\u203c\ufe0f\nThis LinkedIn page Bosch Security and Safety Systems is no longer active.\nTo continue receiving updates and insights on our products, please follow our dedicated LinkedIn pages that are now part of Keenfinity Group:\n\u00b7\u00a0Video Systems \ud83d\udc49 IQSIGHT\n\u00b7\u00a0Intrusion & Access Systems \ud83d\udc49 Radionix\n\u00b7\u00a0Conference Solutions \ud83d\udc49 Conference solutions | Keenfinity Group\n\u00b7\u00a0Public Address Systems \ud83d\udc49 Public Address & Voice Alarm | Keenfinity Group\nThank you for being part of our community here. We look forward to staying connected with you on LinkedIn.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/bosch-security-systems/home/"},{"date":"2026-07-11","text":"Trusted worldwide. Built for what matters.\nThe transition from Bosch Video Systems to IQSIGHT is officially complete.\nWhile our name has changed, the foundation remains the same: more than 60 years of engineering excellence, trusted products, global expertise, and a commitment to helping organizations operate safely, securely, and without interruption.\nFrom everyday operations to mission-critical environments, we deliver reliable, intelligence-first video solutions that perform.\nWelcome to the next chapter. Stay connected with us here > https://lnkd.in/gjd8fz9U","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/bosch-security-systems/home/"},{"date":"2026-07-11","text":"Final reminder: Public Address and Voice Alarm content continues on our dedicated page.\nThis will be our final PAVA-related post on this channel!\nFrom now on, Public Address and Voice Alarm content will continue on the dedicated Public Address & Voice Alarm LinkedIn page.\nThe page is active, focused and built for technical consultants, system integrators, specifiers, project engineers and other professionals working with PAVA systems.\nThank you for following the PAVA conversation here. We look forward to continuing it with you on the dedicated page. See you there?\n\ud83d\udc49 https://lnkd.in/dDcDKfU7\n#BoschPublicAddress #PRAESENSA #PublicAddressandVoiceAlarm #VoiceAlarm #Countdown","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/bosch-security-systems/home/"},{"date":"2026-07-11","text":"We're moving all Conference Systems updates to our \ud835\uddf1\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddf1\ud835\uddf6\ud835\uddf0\ud835\uddee\ud835\ude01\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddf1 #Conference Solutions \ud835\udddf\ud835\uddf6\ud835\uddfb\ud835\uddf8\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddf1\ud835\udddc\ud835\uddfb \ud835\uddfd\ud835\uddee\ud835\uddf4\ud835\uddf2.\nBy following our conference solutions page, you'll receive updates on audio innovation, meeting management, industry trends, events, and product developments, all in one place.\nNo unrelated content. Just the conference solutions that matter to your work.\nFollow today and stay up to date with the latest developments via link in comment.\n#BoschConferenceSystems #ConferenceSystems #KeenfinityGroup #AVTech #BusinessCommunication","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/bosch-security-systems/home/"},{"date":"2026-07-11","text":"Where will you get your PAVA content after June 30?\nThis Bosch Safety and Security channel is closing at the end of the month!\nIf you follow this page for Public Address and Voice Alarm content, please follow the dedicated Public Address & Voice Alarm LinkedIn page now.\nThat is where Bosch PAVA-related product updates, system design content, standards-related guidance and application insights will continue.\nTwo weeks left. The follow takes only a few seconds.\n\ud83d\udc49 https://lnkd.in/dDcDKfU7\n#BoschPublicAddress #Countdown","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/bosch-security-systems/home/"}]}
