## 2026-10-25T22:14:34Z ASIS
{"slug":"ASIS","companyName":"ASIS International","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international","fetchedAt":"2026-10-25T22:14:34Z","followerCount":102629,"bio":"The world's largest association for security professionals, ASIS International has 243 chapters around the globe. Wherever you are in your career, whether just getting started or a seasoned security professional, ASIS International has the tools, information, and global network you need to achieve your goals. Put the power of ASIS to work for you.  www.asisonline.org","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-03-05","text":"Our #MyASIS community is unmatched. We are in awe of our members\u2019 dedication to the profession and each other, who are always looking for ways to support their colleagues and friends. In honor of Membership Appreciation Month we ask that you share your appreciation for your fellow members, maybe someone who has influenced your career or helped you in your ASIS journey? Tag a member in the comments below and be entered to win a FREE GSX All-Access Pass to #GSX2026. #ASISMemberAppreciation","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"Deepfakes, synthetic identities, and targeted phishing are putting pressure on financial institutions. On 4 November, Security Solutions Spotlight: Banking & Finance brings you practical strategies to strengthen your banking and finance security posture, with insights from the sector\u2019s foremost experts.\nExpect four live sessions, each followed by Q&A. Free for members and nonmembers.\nRegister now: https://bit.ly/4jowxiG\n#ASISInternational #Deepfakes #FraudPrevention #FinancialServices","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-24","text":"How are cities moving from reactive, manual investigations to real-time, data-driven public safety, and how is the same infrastructure making them smarter, not just safer?\nGet the answers from Nathan Hale and Brian Ison, CPP, CFE during ASIS\u2019s next webinar, Securing the Future: Cities Across North America.\nExpect standout moments, hard numbers, and an honest look at what separates the cities that are getting it right: open platforms, community trust, and technology deployed as part of a plan.\nFree to all | Registration required\nThursday, 29 October 2026 | 12:30 pm ET | 1 CPE\nSponsored by Milestone Systems\nRegister now: https://lnkd.in/egqk4nYr\n#SmartCity #PublicSafety #RealTimeCrime #ASISInternational","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-23","text":"Violent incidents remain low compared to previous years, but organizations aren\u2019t letting their guard down. In a new ASIS and Everbridge study, less than half of respondents  are highly or mostly confident their staff know what to do in an active assailant incident.\nThe research points to four factors linked to higher confidence in an organization\u2019s preparedness: a comprehensive plan, regular drills, communications technology, and an effective behavioral threat assessment and management (BTAM) team.\nRead the full Security Management article: https://bit.ly/4zHrXkj\nAuthor: Scott Briscoe\n#ASISInternational #ThreatAssessment #BTAM #EmergencyManagement #WorkplaceSafety","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-20","text":"IT sets policies that affect your team with minimal input. Compliance findings surface issues you couldn\u2019t see. Change windows follow IT\u2019s timelines, not yours.\nThe gap between physical security and IT is a governance and communication problem, made worse by limited visibility into the device estate. Join this session to learn how physical security leaders can close that gap by leading the conversations on device ownership, visibility, and governance.\nFree to all | Registration required\nThursday, 22 October 2026 | 12:30 pm ET | 1 CPE\nRegister now: https://bit.ly/4BmlOvN\nSpeaker: Roy Dagan\nSponsored by SecuriThings\n#ASISInternational","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"}]}

## 2026-10-25T22:13:53Z NZSA
{"slug":"NZSA","companyName":"New Zealand Security Association (NZSA)","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/new-zealand-security-association","fetchedAt":"2026-10-25T22:13:53Z","followerCount":3730,"bio":"The New Zealand Security Association (NZSA) is the largest industry representative body for the security industry in New Zealand and represents over 85% of the industry by revenue. Its voluntary members include security providers ranging from large multi-nationals to sole traders and also includes individuals and companies who are not direct providers of security services but have an interest in the industry.\nThe stated objective of the New Zealand Security Association is to do all things necessary and lawful to ensure there is always available to the New Zealand public, a security industry comprising of persons and firms who are fit and proper. The New Zealand Security Association is committed to the highest standards of professional and ethical conduct at all times.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-19","text":"And the last (but by no means least) in our series of Security Awards winners' spotlights shines on Rick Warin. Congratulations Rick!\nView the full list of winners here: https://lnkd.in/eqUpkuCg","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/new-zealand-security-association/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-15","text":"A great event to put in the calendar from our friends at ASIS New Zealand!\nReck R.\n\u2022 3rd+\nSRMP\u2013C | Security Consultant of the Year (2026)\nBook an appointment\nOct 12 \u2022 Edited\nBig news for ASIS New Zealand\nWe are honoured to announce that Hon. Mark Mitchell, Minister for Police, Corrections, and Emergency Management, will be joining us at the next ASIS NZ Chapter meeting this October\nAs New Zealand navigates evolving law-and-order priorities, keeping pace with policy updates is no longer just a compliance task, it is a strategic necessity for security executives, risk leaders, and operational managers alike.\nWhether you\u2019re a security executive, risk leader, or operational manager, staying ahead of legislative change is a strategic necessity.\nTo make sense of it all, we\u2019ve put together an exclusive dual-keynote lineup:\n\ud83c\udfa4 Hon. Mark Mitchell \u2013 Minister for Police, Corrections, and Emergency Management. Bringing direct insights into recent legislative changes, policy shifts, and national saf","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/new-zealand-security-association/home/"}]}

## 2026-10-25T22:13:13Z ASISNZ
{"slug":"ASISNZ","companyName":"ASIS New Zealand","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-new-zealand","fetchedAt":"2026-10-25T22:13:13Z","followerCount":134,"bio":"ASIS New Zealand is a high level security integrator company based out of Wellington and Auckland, New Zealand.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-25","text":"Happy Labour Day to every worker across New Zealand, and especially to the security professionals who help keep people, property, and communities safe.\nOur work is essential, and many in the security industry will not have the luxury of taking the day off.\nWhile others rest, travel, and spend time with loved ones, security stand ready for the next job.\nToday, we want to acknowledge and thank all ASIS New Zealand Security employees, as well as our colleagues here in New Zealand and in Australia at ADT Security Australia, ADT Security New Zealand , Wormald NZ , ACG Integration - (Australia), Signature Security Group, Intelligent Monitoring Solutions and Intelligent Monitoring Group Limited \u2013 along with security professionals and workers around the world.\nYour commitment, professionalism, and hard work do not go unnoticed.\nIf you are fortunate enough to have the day off, we hope you enjoy it with your wh\u0101nau.\n#LabourDay #SecurityProfessionals #ProtectingWhatMatters #KeepingCommunitiesSafe #Essent","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-new-zealand/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"It's been just over a month since R. was awarded Security Consultant of the Year at the New Zealand Security Association, and we're still proud of what this achievement represents.\nCombined with Shamal Kumar's recognition as a finalist, it highlights the depth of talent across the ASIS New Zealand team and our commitment to delivering great outcomes for our clients.\nThanks NZSA, Gary Morrison, Lucy Nichols, Tacia Strawbridge, and everyone else involved in making this incredible event possible.\nWell done again, team.\n#NZSA #SecurityAwards #TeamASISNZ #SecurityConsultant #NewZealand #ASISNZHighLevelSecurity","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-new-zealand/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-20","text":"What do you think is the biggest physical security gap in NZ businesses right now?\nCast your vote below, then tell us why in the comments. We'd love to hear what's happening in your industry and whether you've seen this challenge firsthand.\nWe'll publish the findings and our take next week","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-new-zealand/home/"},{"date":"2026-09-12","text":"Well done to our very own Reck R. for winning security consultant of the year at the New Zealand Security Association awards night last night, definitely deserved! Also a huge congratulations to Shamal Kumar from our team for being a finalist also! Well done team! Congratulations to everyone who won awards and finalists!","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-new-zealand/home/"},{"date":"2026-08-12","text":"Well done team!\nReck R.\n\u2022 3rd+\nSRMP\u2013C | Security Consultant of the Year (2026)\nBook an appointment\nAug 12 \u2022 Edited\nThe day started with fantastic news! I\u2019m proud to share that Shamal Kumar and I have been selected as finalists for the New Zealand Security Association Awards.\n\u200bA h-u-g-e thank you to our incredible team at ASIS New Zealand High Level Security and the executive at ASIS New Zealand for enabling me to do my work.\n\u200bMore than anyone else, I want to thank my partner, Jay R. , for helping me become a better person on both a personal and professional level.\n\u200b\nCongrats to Shamal and all the other finalists. Looking forward to the awards night!\nCustomer Champion\nChelsea Wallis \u2013 Optic Security Group\nRebecca Magee \u2013 Armourguard Security\nSu Kaur \u2013 FIRST Security\nDesign and Support Electronic Sector Professional\nBartho Huyser \u2013 Optic Security\nDaniel Malan \u2013 Global Security Solutions Limited Ltd\nSimon Paul \u2013 ICE Security Limited\nElectronic Security Trainee\nBrynn Lightfoot \u2013 Nelson Alarms Secu","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-new-zealand/home/"}]}
